    "result_text": "Done. The only test class in the suite (`AcceptanceTest`) is green, and the full `mvn test` build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required returning `checkDigit` = a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. Since `checkDigit` is a derived, read-only field (like `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `identityKey`, etc.), I followed the existing derived-field pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (integer, 0\u20139), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(toCheckDigit(owner))\")` to `toOwnerDto`, plus a `toCheckDigit` helper that computes the standard Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode` (ignoring the `-` separators), returning `null` when no code is present.\n\nThe `checkDigit` is derived at read time from the stored `customerCode`, so it stays consistent on both create and fetch. The acceptance test \u2014 which recomputes Luhn independently from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 passes.",
