    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThis change is a clean, additive extension of the mapper's existing pattern. `OwnerMapper` already derives read-time fields via `@Mapping(expression = \"java(...)\")` paired with `default` methods (`toContactPreference`, `toIdentityKey`), and `toCheckDigit` follows that structure exactly: same annotation style, a private-ish `default` helper on the interface, and a javadoc that mirrors the tone of the neighboring `toIdentityKey` doc. A maintainer of this codebase would find the new method sitting right where the other owner-derivation helpers live, which is natural.\n\n- The logic is in the right unit given the established convention \u2014 read-time derived DTO fields are computed in the mapper here, not scattered elsewhere, so this is consistent rather than a new catch-all responsibility.\n- No duplication: the Luhn computation doesn't exist elsewhere in the diff's context, and nothing else needs it.\n- The OpenAPI schema addition (`checkDigit`, int32, 0\u20139, `readOnly`, with description matching the javadoc) is the correct companion change and stays coherent with the code.\n\nThe Luhn loop itself is self-contained and doesn't bloat the interface beyond the one derivation it owns.",
